I don't know, I still have the impression that those bonuses count for
a bit less in 3rd edition relative to opponents.  I could be wrong on
this though.

> I think this might be a good spot to raise the question: How much do
> stats really matter in Nethack, after a certain point?  (Assume we're
> discussing vanilla here.)

Constitution is one of the best stats if it's earned -early-, since
CON gains later on don't add hit points retroactively.  Strength's
carry bonus is still significant even with a bag of holding; I
typically play without a stash, and if I make good decisions about
what to carry, bless the bag, and get strength to 18, I can usually go
around unburdened.

I think the problem with stats is that, not counting problems caused
by very low scores, even the maximum bonus doesn't amount to much.

I still say the stat cap should be raised.  Either that or stat points
made a bit harder to max out.  As it is I typically max out all stats
before ascending without really trying.  Exercuse, unicorn use to
offset negative exercise and other losses, and a few blessed potions
of gain ability is typically enough to do it.

